## Instructions

Address each review comment. Make ALL the necessary code changes first, then **`git add` and `git commit` everything as a SINGLE commit before finishing.** Do not create one commit per comment, and do not leave any uncommitted work. The commit message should summarize the whole feedback round.

Do NOT reference the issue number (e.g. `{{ issue_ref }}`) in commit messages — the commits are visible in the PR, and issue references clutter the issue timeline.
Do NOT push — the orchestrator handles pushing.

Your final message will be posted on the PR as a reply to the reviewer. Write it for them: briefly state, per comment, what you changed (or why you disagree, if you didn't make a change). Keep it concise — no restating of the comments, no file dumps.
